SECTION 1 — IDENTITY DOCUMENTS (Required for all claimants)

  [ ] 1a. Valid government-issued photo ID
           (Driver's license, state ID card, or passport)

  [ ] 1b. If name on deed/records differs from current legal name:
           — Certified copy of marriage certificate, divorce decree,
             or court order showing name change

SECTION 2 — PROOF OF INTEREST IN PROPERTY

  For Former Owners:
  [ ] 2a. Copy of the recorded grant deed or deed by which you
           acquired title (obtained from the county recorder)
  [ ] 2b. Any documents showing you held title at time of tax sale
  [ ] 2c. Copies of any property tax bills or statements in your name

  For Lienholders / Deed of Trust Holders:
  [ ] 2d. Certified copy of the recorded deed of trust or mortgage
  [ ] 2e. Copy of the promissory note (if available)
  [ ] 2f. Payoff statement or evidence of outstanding balance at
           time of tax sale (if available)

  For Judgment Creditors:
  [ ] 2g. Certified copy of the recorded abstract of judgment
  [ ] 2h. Evidence that judgment was recorded before the tax sale date

SECTION 3 — PROOF OF CURRENT ADDRESS / CONTACT

  [ ] 3a. Utility bill, bank statement, or official mail showing
           current mailing address (dated within 60 days)

SECTION 4 — AUTHORIZATION (if using a representative)

  [ ] 4a. Signed and notarized Power of Attorney or written
           authorization designating your representative
           (exact form required by {{ county_name }} — VERIFY WITH COUNTY)

SECTION 5 — ADDITIONAL DOCUMENTS (county-specific — VERIFY)

  [ ] 5a. Completed county claim form
           (Obtain from {{ county_agency }} — REQUIRES VERIFICATION)
  [ ] 5b. Any other documentation requested by the county

